# Line-ending policy for this repo.
#
# thirdparty/ (QCBOR, libriscv) is vendored via git subtree at
# exact upstream fork commits (see README.md). Any normalization there
# would diff it away from that pinned commit, including its own native
# Windows project files (*.sln, *.vcxproj, *.ps1). Exempt it completely:
# -text disables all of git's line-ending handling for these paths, so
# checkout/checkin never touches a single byte.
thirdparty/** -text

# Everything this repo actually owns: normalize to LF on checkin
# regardless of what line ending a given checkout produced, and check
# out as LF. This is a Linux/POSIX server codebase; CRLF has no reason
# to appear here outside the vendored dirs above.
*.c text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.hpp text eol=lf
*.cc text eol=lf
CMakeLists.txt text eol=lf
*.cmake text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.js text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.gd text eol=lf
*.tscn text eol=lf
*.godot text eol=lf

# Binary, never subject to any text handling.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.a binary
*.so binary
